+/*
+ * Software job queue, a ring of 1..PEND_MAX parked jobs (patch 0227, T-e395 one slot, T-b1c0 ring; boot-arg sweetmalipend=N, 0 = default OFF = behaviour unchanged). Today
+ * sweet_mali_submit blocks its caller until the previous job is done (strictly one job in flight), so backboardd's GL thread sleeps 5.1-5.9 ms per frame (SWAPT wait_us p50) and cannot
+ * build the next job meanwhile. With the knob on, a submit that finds one job in flight and fewer than N parked parks its job in the ring (seqno assigned now, FIFO) and returns at
+ * once; finish() starts the oldest parked job right after the running job completes, with EXACTLY the register writes and clean-slot check of the direct path (sm_start_locked): still
+ * one job on the hardware at any time, same order, same slots, no new register or value. sweetmalipend=1 is the T-e395 one-slot behaviour. If the running job failed, faulted or the
+ * device died, EVERY parked job behind it is DROPPED (a dependent fragment job must not run behind a failed tiler job): each is marked failed (fail_seq, so sweet_mali_wait returns
+ * EIO) and printed as `SWEET MALI GAP: queued job ... dropped`. A submit finding the ring full blocks as before.
+ * Lifetime: boClose/unmap wait for the client's last seqno (SweetMali.cpp fLastSeq) and seq_next counts queued jobs, so a BO is never unmapped under a queued job.
